1|# GUIDE 01 — Worktree-cap exhaustion loop (`WORKTREE_CAP_REACHED`)
2|
3|Cause 1 in `WIDE_NET_ANALYSIS.md`. All 49 reasoned interrupts fleet-wide carry
4|`Reason: Runner workdir unavailable: Worktree cap reached (~5); ...` — this is
5|the only cause with direct textual proof in task histories.
6|
7|- **Verdict: REPLICABLE-LOCALLY.** The cap logic is pure filesystem code
8|  (`runner/project.js`), and the backend reaction is unit-testable with mock
9|  stores. No prod, no agents.
10|- **Code seams:** `runner/project.js:33` (`WORKTREE_CAP = 5`),
11|  `runner/project.js:34` (`WORKTREE_EVICT_STALE_MS = 30 min`),
12|  `prepareWorkdir` refusal at `runner/project.js:1185-1199`,
13|  `listOrphanWorkdirs` at `runner/project.js:424`,
14|  daemon catch at `runner/daemon.js:2299-2314` (interrupt WITH reason, no
15|  rethrow, keeps polling), backend counter at
16|  `api/flow/executionLedger.js` (`interruptExecution`,
17|  `MAX_RUNNER_INTERRUPTS = 5` at `:17`), park rule at
18|  `api/flow/scheduler/isAutoResumableWithReason.js` (`runner-death-loop`).
19|
20|## 1. Signature (recognise it)
21|
22|- Task history rows: `Runner <id> interrupted execution <exec> — lease dropped,
23|  re-queues as interrupted. Reason: Runner workdir unavailable: Worktree cap
24|  reached (~5); ...` — always with a `Reason:` suffix naming the cap.
25|- Timing: interrupt lands seconds after the runner's `started` progress event,
26|  never after `prompted` (refusal happens inside `prepareWorkdir`).
27|- Loop shape: interrupt -> `Auto-resumed after server restart — prioritised
28|  in queue` -> same runner re-claims within ~150 ms -> cap refusal again. On
29|  the 5th consecutive refusal on the same stage the task parks as
30|  `runner-death-loop` (see GUIDE 07 for why a *capacity* problem is counted as
31|  *runner deaths*).
32|- Runner host: work root (e.g. `/home/[REDACTED]/.kainbain` on local-alpha,
33|  `/home/[REDACTED]/.kainbain` on server2-alpha) holds >= 5 live `kb-*`
34|  workdirs, none older than 30 min.
35|
36|## 2. Safe local replication (runner side, `node:test`)
37|
38|Reproduce the refusal with a temp work root holding 5 *fresh* orphan workdirs,
39|then show the stale-eviction escape hatch. Pattern follows
40|`runner/project.test.js` (`localRepo()` helper creates a temp git repo).
